## At a glance

| Dimension | Vellum | Tracify |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **Scope** | Full LLM platform (build, deploy, observe) | Observability + evaluation |
| **Workflows** | Native visual builder | Not included |
| **Deployment** | Built-in | Not included |
| **Evaluation** | Included but not primary | Core feature |
| **Cost tracking** | Basic | Comprehensive |
| **Best for** | Full LLM lifecycle | Agent observability focus |

Vellum is an all-in-one LLM platform; Tracify is specialized observability.

## Core difference

**Vellum** covers *entire LLM lifecycle*: build workflows, deploy to production, observe results. **Tracify** specializes in *observability and evaluation*: understand agent behavior and iterate.

These serve different needs.

## Scenario 1: building and deploying LLM workflows

You want to build workflows visually, deploy them, and observe results all in one place.

**With Vellum:** Visual workflows, deployment, observability all integrated.

**With Tracify:** Observability only, workflows require external tools.

**Result:** Vellum wins on completeness.

## Scenario 2: observing existing agents

You have agents already deployed and need deep observability and evaluation.

**With Vellum:** Works but not optimized for multi-turn, complex agents.

**With Tracify:** Purpose-built for agent observability at scale.

**Result:** Tracify wins on focus and depth.

## Cost and scope

**Vellum:** Full platform, higher price, all-in-one
**Tracify:** Observability only, lower price, focused

If you need full LLM platform, Vellum. If you need observability for existing systems, Tracify.

## When to choose each

**Choose Vellum:** If you need full LLM platform (build + deploy + observe)
**Choose Tracify:** If observability is your primary need

